Z||000000||fierosound||01-25-2000||01:55 AM||||I liked the look of the LCARS (Library Computer Access And Retrieval) computer screens on Star Trek right from the time they were introduced in the Star Trek movies.  I always thought it'd be neat to have a desktop that looked like it.  There are many suitable wallpapers that can be used, but I wanted something that wasn't "static".  Below is a screen shot of an Active Desktop wallpaper I've put togther.  Three of the screens are animated - a rotating Enterprise, flying through space viewscreen and digital number readouts.  I've also put together a Star Trek theme which utilizes Star Trek Computer WAVs for all Windows functions.  It get alot of great comments.  It is set up for a 1024x768 screen.  I can email to anyone here who like it.  Please state whether you'd like the Active Desktop or Theme (or both).  Any other trekkers out there??<P>    <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound/trek.jpg">    <P>PS - the best site for Star Trek is <A HREF="http://www.treksearch.com" TARGET=_blank>www.treksearch.com</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 01-25-2000).]||||reg||6
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||01-25-2000||02:12 AM||||That desktop looks awesome!! A bit too complicated for my tastes tho. my background is mostly plain black.<P>I'm not much of a trekkie anymore, but I still watch voyager every wed. night, and I used to watch TNG & DS9 as well..<P>Regarding sci-fi, I'm more into Star Wars now, but I'll always like trek.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
